From 38d379418c4bcdaf186646c6816ee4402f2d44b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Allen Pomeroy <allen@pomeroy.us>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:18:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Never allocate clusters at or past the end of the volume
 (SCB$L_VOLSIZE)

The allocator searched every bit in BITMAP.SYS, including the bits past the
last cluster in the bitmap's last block and a partial last cluster. Where
those bits read free, a run there mapped LBNs at or beyond the volume's end:
on a SIMH container that overwrites the metadata footer and grows the image.
VMS INITIALIZE marks them allocated, so this did not happen on the 8 GB
volume, but nothing on the write path now depends on it: the search is
limited to clusters wholly inside SCB$L_VOLSIZE. tests/cli_volume_end_check.sh
fails 6/6 on the old code and passes with this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WA1cTvnJjW7a9acesLHq2C
